Widen the title-bar close-box hit region.

The close glyph is a single character drawn at column f->e.x-2, and the hit
test required an exact match on that one cell. A single 8px cell is a tiny
target: on a HiDPI host it is 16 physical pixels, and a click that lands one
cell to either side of the glyph silently does nothing. Accept the whole
close gadget zone (xe-3 .. xe-1) so clicking on or immediately beside the
glyph dismisses the dialog. The maximize gadget sits at xe-4 and is checked
separately, so the widened range does not swallow it.

diff --git a/we_mouse.c b/we_mouse.c
index 5ef78cd..b06fe38 100644
--- a/we_mouse.c
+++ b/we_mouse.c
@@ -187,7 +187,7 @@ static int e_hit_close_button(FENSTER *f)
 {
  extern struct mouse e_mouse;
  if (e_mouse.y != f->a.y) return 0;
- return e_mouse.x == f->e.x - 2;
+ return e_mouse.x >= f->e.x - 3 && e_mouse.x <= f->e.x - 1;
 }

 static int e_hit_maximize_button(FENSTER *f)
